WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.568
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.969
This is "Late Night." We hope
you're doing well tonight.

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.106
And now, if you don't mind,
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.775
Well, there are just
15 days left in 2021,

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:14.247
and by my calculations, it
leaves two more years of 2020.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.949
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.516
When asked
by reporters yesterday

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:19.852
if his Build Back Better act
will pass Congress

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.053
by the end of the year,

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.489
President Biden said,
"It's gonna be close."

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.659
Buddy, it's December 16th.
It's already close.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.727
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.929
At this point,
even Amazon Prime's like,

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.698
"How's March?"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.667
President Biden
and Vice President Kamala Harris

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.436
met with members
of the White House

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.838
Coronavirus Response Team today
to discuss the omicron variant,

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:43.075
which was pretty awkward,
considering it was right there

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.477
in the room with them.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:49.448
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.918
I didn't know
it got such a good seat.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.219
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.287
According to new data,
an initial symptom

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.256
of the omicron
coronavirus variant

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:58.725
may be a scratchy throat.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.794
Oh, man, then I wouldn't
get so close, Little Steven.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:05.030
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.234
And I want you all
to realize that I do know --

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.337
In back-to-back jokes, I went
"ahm-icron" and "oh-micron."

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.905
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.741
Just trying
to cover all my bases.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:15.774
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:17.410
Hope you're all happy.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.845
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.814
NASA announced this week
that its Parker Solar Probe

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.550
became the first spacecraft
in history to touch the sun.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.986
And if you want to get some idea
of the intensity

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:30.023
of that kind of heat,
microwave a burrito.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.325
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:35.495
The Biden administration this
week reversed a Trump-era rule

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.564
allowing more powerful
shower heads.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:40.667
Well, there goes
the divorced-aunt vote.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.436
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.772
I say "ont."

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.440
I get a lot of grief around here
for saying "ont."

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.243
Shoemaker, our producer,
always tells me it's "ant,"

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.511
and yesterday,
we had Marisa Tomei on the show,

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.113
and he told me,
'cause she's in "Spider-Man"

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.782
and she plays Aunt May, and
he's like, "It's not 'ont' May.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:00.420
Like, don't embarrass yourself."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.422
"It's 'ant' May,
and you do that all the time."

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.590
And then he said,
"And even worse,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.326
Paul Rudd is not 'ont'-Man."

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.294
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.630
Which I guess I had been doing.
I didn't even realize.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.732
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.967
Former First Lady Melania Trump
announced today

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.169
that she will launch
a new NFT platform,

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:20.340
which is crazy 'cause I always
thought she was one.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.440
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.943
"Wait. I think
that NFT just blinked."

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.110
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.113
And finally,
experts are projecting that

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.215
"Paw Patrol" toys
will be a popular

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.083
children's Christmas gift
this year.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:34.954
It's the gift that'll have
your nephew saying, "I'm 13!"

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.756
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:40.326
"Do better, 'ont'-Man!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.428
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

